In your case, you want to test that the `cannotBeNull` function correctly asserts that `param` is not null. The callback you provide to `expect` should return a boolean value indicating whether the assertion was successful.

Here's how you can modify your code to make it work:

```dart
void cannotBeNull(dynamic param) {
  assert(param != null);
}

void main() {
  test('cannoBeNull assertion', () {
    expect(cannotBeNull(null), throwsAssertionError);
  });
}

// Alternatively, if you're using Flutter:
void main() {
  test('cannoBeNull assertion', () {
    expect(cannotBeNull(null), throwsA<AssertionError>());
  });
}
```

