samples.second_piece:
When leaving out generic parameters, almost all of the generics logic is skipped. Determining the type of T will not be 'smart' and just look at the way T is defined within that class/interface. If you want to use the generics logic, you should provide generic parameters instead of leaving them out - they can still be very, well, 'generic':

