How to make a Drupal 7 temporary cache item expire after a certain time?

The `cache_set` function in Drupal 7 doesn't automatically expire a cache item after a certain amount of time. You need to explicitly set the `expire` field to a specific time in seconds.

Here's how you can modify your function to make it expire after 30 seconds:

```php
function mymodule_get_something($id) {
  // set the unique cache id
  $cid = 'id-'. $id;

  // return data if there's an un-expired cache entry
  //  *** $cache ALWAYS gets populated with my expired data
  if ($cache = cache_get($cid, 'cache_mymodule')) {
    return $cache->data;
  }

  // set the cache to expire after 30 seconds
  cache_set($cid, $something, 'cache_mymodule', time() + 30);

  // return my data
  return $something;
}
```

With this change, the cache item with the unique ID `id-1` will expire after 30 seconds.

